// ============================================================================
// THE ONE-SHOT BACKFILL — the record of how provenance/register.json was made
// on 2026-08-04. IT IS NOT PART OF THE GATE AND MUST NOT BE RE-RUN TO ABSORB
// NEW CONTENT.
// ============================================================================
// If a future round re-runs this over strings that did not exist today, every
// rule below silently swallows them and the boundary stops being a boundary.
// New content gets a row written for it, deliberately, one row at a time. This
// file exists so the 2026-08-04 classification can be AUDITED — every rule
// carries the evidence it rests on — not so it can be repeated.
//
// THE DEFAULT IS INVENTION. A string no rule matches is not blessed, it is
// FLAGGED. That is the only default that is safe: a backfill whose fallback is
// "probably fine" is the failure it was written to fix.
//
// WHAT THE CLASSIFICATION IS AND IS NOT. It records THE PROVENANCE THIS
// REPOSITORY ALREADY STATES — a fact's own `source:` tag, a card's own
// `Verified` row, an accession number, a photograph on file, a quoted ruling in
// a file header, a clause of THE_CHARTER. It does NOT independently re-verify
// those sources. "VERIFIED" on a row means the repo carries a citation for it
// and names it; it does not mean anybody re-read Wikipedia today.
//
//   node provenance/backfill-20260804.mjs --write

